# G077 — Remote SQL Tool

*v2. See `remote-sql-tool.md` for prose: transaction envelope with
explicit begin/commit/rollback, in-memory relational schema,
parameterized queries.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Vault Notes Database

[vault-notes-db
    IN ORDER TO
        persist and search markdown notes in a relational schema
        using transactions for write batches

    @conn <- [db[connect]]
    [db[create-table {conn: @conn, name: "notes",
                       columns: [{name: "id", type: "int"}
                                  {name: "title", type: "text"}
                                  {name: "body", type: "text"}
                                  {name: "created_at", type: "int"}]}]]

    sync @user-events {
        save @title @body ->
            [db[begin {conn: @conn}]]
            [db[insert {conn: @conn, table: "notes",
                         values: [[clock[now]], @title, @body, [clock[now]]]}]]
            [db[commit {conn: @conn}]]
                || [db[rollback {conn: @conn}]]

        search @query ->
            @results <- [db[select {conn: @conn,
                                     query: {table: "notes",
                                             columns: ["id", "title"],
                                             where: "body LIKE ?",
                                             params: ["%" + @query + "%"]}}]]
            #results @results
    }
]

---

## Verb Surface

[db
    connect
    create-table    {conn, name, columns}
    insert          {conn, table, values}       ;; || exec-error
    begin           {conn}
    commit          {conn}                       ;; || exec-error
    rollback        {conn}
    select          {conn, query}                ;; || exec-error
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: transaction as begin/commit/|| rollback

[begin]
    ...writes...
[commit]
    || [rollback]

The `||` fulfillment ensures rollback happens on any resistance
within the transaction body. The v1 try/catch pattern dissolves into
native fulfillment.

---

## Demo

[demo
    @conn <- [db[connect]]
    [db[create-table {conn: @conn, name: "users",
                       columns: [{name: "id", type: "int"}
                                  {name: "name", type: "text"}]}]]

    [db[begin {conn: @conn}]]
    [db[insert {conn: @conn, table: "users", values: [1, "Alice"]}]]
    [db[insert {conn: @conn, table: "users", values: [2, "Bob"]}]]
    [db[commit {conn: @conn}]]

    -> [db[select {conn: @conn,
                    query: {table: "users", columns: ["name"],
                            where: "id = ?", params: [1]}}]]
    ;; -> [["Alice"]]
]
